{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790429220,"nonce":"m8BU8ld3m70lr1qMAlKIY9wrbjA=","title":"wasm: one runtime object with Ash, caribou and the adapters; the seam filled by a static constructor","message":"Ash links a wasm program against one prelinked relocatable object,\nash_runtime.o: ash_std as a staticlib, joined with wasi libc and\nlibsetjmp by rust-lld -r (scripts/build_wasm_runtime.py). The linker\n(ash_wasm_link, called from aot_link::link_wasm_module) takes the\nprogram's objects plus that one runtime; `ASH_RUNTIME` or the runtime\nargument names another one.\n\nCaribou's version:\n- One staticlib crate depending on ash_std, caribou, caribou-ash\n  (without its runner), caribou-wren and WrenLift's runtime half. It\n  must be one staticlib: two copies of a runtime's exports do not link.\n- Prelinked the same way, with Ash's force-included libc list, and\n  handed to Ash's link step as the runtime.\n- The seam: natively the driver calls hlp_rt_install at run time. On\n  AOT and wasm, a constructor in the object calls it. The module's start\n  section runs __wasm_call_ctors at instantiation, and .init_array runs\n  before main natively, so the install lands before the entry point's\n  hlp_gc_init creates the heap. hlp_rt_install refuses once the heap\n  exists.\n\nDone: caribou-ash builds for wasm32-wasip1. trap.c gets LLVM's wasm\nsetjmp lowering, as Ash's code does.","files":null}]}